\[
H_{\rm low}=KD+\delta H_{4,S}^C+O(\delta\epsilon^2),\qquad
H_{\rm high}\ge \frac{\delta}{2\epsilon^4}.
\]
The low block is uniformly lower bounded because \(D\ge0\) and \(H_{4,S}^C\) is uniformly bounded.

For arbitrary positive microscopic density \(\rho\), write
\(r=U^*\rho U\), \(w=\operatorname{Tr}Qr\), \(p=1-w\), and
