The high energy is nonnegative, so
\[
\operatorname{Tr}(h_S\sigma)
\le \frac{E_{\rm fast}+O(\delta\epsilon^2)}p
\le E_{\rm fast}+O_{E_{\rm cap}}(\epsilon^2).
\]
Both the lower bound and upper cap on \(E_{\rm fast}\) justify the second normalization step, including negative energies. This bounds \(\operatorname{Tr}D\sigma\); the form estimate then gives
\[
\operatorname{Tr}(h\sigma)\le E_{\rm fast}+O_{E_{\rm cap}}(\epsilon).
